\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{The internal factor of a lattice Dirac operator}
\date{2026-11-13}

\p{Mathematical physics writes #{\Gamma_j=\gamma_j\otimes I_F}, a
gamma matrix on the spinor factor and an identity on the internal
factor. By the relation in the [centered Dirac operator](fdip-000R), that generator is
#{\varepsilon_j^{S}} on the spinor factor and #{\bbI_F} on the
internal factor. The internal representation in this definition
is already #{\rho}, and the grid step is already #{e_j}.}
